   "project": "Apache Arrow Go v18.7.0",
   "finding": "no allocator promises an alignment: `NewGoAllocator` buffers inherit Go's 8 KiB spans, so a buffer starts at offset 0 or 8192 within a 16 KiB page and page-aligned import is a coin flip whose odds depend on heap fragmentation (measured between 5/20 and 15/20 across runs); `memory/mallocator` (libc, `NewMallocatorWithAlignment`) does give a chosen alignment, which the report as first written missed, so the remaining ask is the documentation. Related and already closed: [apache/arrow-go#70](https://github.com/apache/arrow-go/issues/70) (the C Data Interface storing unpinned Go pointers, which `runtime.Pinner` addresses)",
   "repo": "apache/arrow-go",
   "number": 1297,
   "url": "https://github.com/apache/arrow-go/issues/1297",
   "kind": "issue",
   "title": "[Memory] No allocator documents an alignment: NewGoAllocator buffers land at offset 0 or 8192 within a 16 KiB page, so page-aligned handoff to C is chance",
   "reporter": "singhpratech",
   "reported": "2026-09-08",
   "state": "fixed",
   "closed_at": "2026-09-08T19:18:38Z",
   "labels": [
