     "at": "2026-09-08T04:13:54Z",
     "actor": "lidavidm",
     "association": "member",
     "text": "I believe it's not safe to share a Go-allocated buffer with C anyways (at least persistently, without pinning). https://pkg.go.dev/cmd/cgo#hdr-Passing_pointers As the referenced issue states, you should use mallocator for this, or you would need an allocator that also pins buffer…",
     "url": "https://github.com/apache/arrow-go/issues/1297#issuecomment-5579080928"
    },
    {
     "type": "comment",
     "at": "2026-09-08T16:44:24Z",
     "actor": "zeroshade",
     "association": "member",
     "text": "> If a short paragraph in the memory package doc, pointing at mallocator and NewMallocatorWithAlignment for buffers that C will keep, would be welcome, I am glad to open a pull request; otherwise please feel free to close this. It would absolutely be welcome! Please do!",
     "url": "https://github.com/apache/arrow-go/issues/1297#issuecomment-5588655786"
    },
